<statement>
<p>
Determine which matrices are in reduced row echelon form, which others are only in row echelon form, and which are not in row echelon form.</p>
<p>
<m>\displaystyle{\left[\begin{array}{cccc} {1}\amp{0}\amp{1}\amp{0}\\{0}\amp{1}\amp{1}\amp{0}\\{0}\amp{0}\amp{0}\amp{1}\end{array}\right]}</m> </p>
<p><ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha"><li>row echelon form</li> 
<li>reduced row echelon form</li> 
<li>not in row echelon form</li> 
</ol></p>
<p>
<m>\displaystyle{\left[\begin{array}{ccccc} {1}\amp{1}\amp{0}\amp{1}\amp{1}\\{0}\amp{6}\amp{0}\amp{6}\amp{6}\\{0}\amp{0}\amp{0}\amp{2}\amp{2}\\{0}\amp{0}\amp{0}\amp{0}\amp{7}\end{array}\right]}</m> </p>
<p><ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha"><li>row echelon form</li> 
<li>reduced row echelon form</li> 
<li>not in row echelon form</li> 
</ol></p>
<p>
<m>\displaystyle{\left[\begin{array}{cccc} {1}\amp{0}\amp{0}\amp{0}\\{0}\amp{1}\amp{0}\amp{0}\\{0}\amp{0}\amp{1}\amp{1}\end{array}\right]}</m> </p>
<p><ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha"><li>row echelon form</li> 
<li>reduced row echelon form</li> 
<li>not in row echelon form</li> 
</ol></p>

</statement>
<answer>
<p><ul><li>B: reduced row echelon form</li><li>C: not in row echelon form</li><li>B: reduced row echelon form</li></ul></p>
</answer>

</myopenmath>